# The prompt is tokenized with Python's GIL released. HF tokenizers' `encode` holds the GIL for the whole text (~1.2 us a
# token), so while a long prompt is tokenized on its request thread, the glm-batch engine thread and every other stream
# wait for the GIL; `encode_batch_fast` on the one text returns the same ids with the GIL released (the binding calls
# `py.allow_threads`) and without the character offsets nothing here reads. Three call sites change:
# - PromptTokens._full (patches/0210): the one tokenizer call a chat or completions request reaches (check() encodes,
#   run() reuses the ids through Memo): a cold prompt in full, a cached prompt's tail after its last shared special token.
# - App.tokenize (patches/0490): POST /tokenize, a string prompt or the rendered messages.
# - App.prompt_ids (patches/0210): unreachable for GLM (GlmApp overrides it, and encodes through PromptTokens); routed
#   through the same helper so no `encode` call is left in server.py.
# Needs tokenizers >= 0.20 (Tokenizer.encode_batch_fast(input, is_pretokenized=False, add_special_tokens=True)); the
# image's transformers 5.17.0 pins tokenizers >= 0.23.1. Host only: same ids, no engine, kernel or token change.
# Idea from MiaAI-Lab/GLM-5.3-Flash-EXL3-2x-DGX-Sparks-TensorFold patch 0099-glm-tokenize-nogil (Apache-2.0; its
# CHANGELOG credits BadAd84), re-implemented for this tree: 0099 does not apply here (0210's PromptTokens and 0490's
# tokenize changed the lines it edits), and its GlmVision.prepare, forced-think-close and call-gate hunks have no
# counterpart (this tree's vision reuses PromptTokens' ids; it has no call gate). In production on two GB10s since
# 2026-10-20 (long-prompt recall checks pass); the same-ids claim rests on 0099's tools/tokenize_check.py, not re-run here.
#
diff --git a/src/tensorfold/cuda/server.py b/src/tensorfold/cuda/server.py
